/* ============================================================================
   FIRST-RUN TIDBIT — the one-card overlay
   Slice 4 of docs/dev-docs/specs/first-run-and-pack-opening.md.

   Self-contained: backdrop, card surface and layout all live here. The Got it
   control wears the host screen's own button classes.
   ============================================================================ */

/* Display, not opacity: an overlay left at opacity 0 still eats every touch on the
   screen behind it, and this one sits over a screen whose only job is to be
   tapped. */
.tidbit-overlay--hidden {
    display: none;
}

/* Full-screen dim that centres the card. UI Toolkit has no z-index: the
   overlay covers the screen because it is the LAST child of the root, and moving
   it up the tree is what would put a screen on top of it.

   If it ever needs inset from the screen edge, use MARGIN on .tidbit-card and not
   padding on the root — #237, padding does not reach absolute children and fails
   by doing nothing. */
.tidbit-overlay {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}

/* 460 rather than the old portrait-era 320px, which stacked the illustration above
   the copy and left no room for it. 460 puts the art beside the words instead.

   460 HAS NOT BEEN RE-MEASURED SINCE THE PANEL CHANGED (#349). It was chosen against
   a 914 x 411 panel, where it was half the width; the panel is 2400 x 1080 authored px
   now, so the same 460 is a fifth of it. The card is the tidbit's whole content, so
   check it on a device before shipping the first tidbit rather than trusting this
   number — it is the older of the two units, not a decision anyone has re-made. */
.tidbit-card {
    width: 460px;
    max-width: 90%;
    background-color: #131A24;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: #263041;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 16px;
}

.tidbit-header {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
}

.tidbit-title {
    font-size: 16px;
    -unity-font-style: bold;
    color: #F2F4F7;
}

/* Art left, copy right. Two lines of body against a 4:3 illustration is the whole
   card, so nothing here scrolls and nothing measures. */
.tidbit-body-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
}

/* 4:3, matching the 800x600 source in spec §6.5. FirstRunTidbit.Render sets
   display: none on this element when the sprite does not resolve, so the copy
   takes the full width rather than sitting beside a hole. */
.tidbit-art {
    width: 176px;
    height: 132px;
    margin-right: var(--space-3);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}

/* flex-basis 0 with grow, so the label wraps to the space left rather than sizing
   itself to its text and pushing the art out of the card. No overflow: hidden —
   a shrinkable flex child with it deletes its children outright in UI Toolkit. */
.tidbit-copy {
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-basis: 0;
    white-space: normal;
    color: #A1A7B3;
}

.tidbit-actions {
    flex-direction: row;
}
